{
  "enabled": true,
  "name": "Test and commit spec task",
  "description": "When a spec task finishes, run npm test. If it passes, commit the task's changes in small commits and log the hashes. If it fails, don't commit.",
  "version": "1",
  "when": {
    "type": "postTaskExecution"
  },
  "then": {
    "type": "askAgent",
    "prompt": "A spec task just finished. 1) Run `npm test`. 2) If tests fail, do NOT commit anything. Explain which tests failed and the likely cause, and stop. 3) If tests pass, follow .kiro/steering/git.md. First run `git branch --show-current`; if it is `main`, do not commit, create the task branch named per git.md and commit there: make one or more small Conventional Commits covering only this task's changes. Stage specific paths with `git add <paths>` (never `git add .` or `-A`), never commit .env files or secrets, add Task/Requirement/Evidence trailers where they apply, and never push. 4) After committing, add the commit hashes (short form) to the matching entry in docs/kiro-log.md, following .kiro/steering/kiro-journal.md. Commit the log update as a separate `docs:` commit. Do not delete or rewrite earlier log entries."
  }
}
